            <ArticleTitle>Acute renal artery aneurysm rupture - a rare differential diagnosis of acute appendicitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>445-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10354-011-0021-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 50-year-old patient with symptoms of an acute appendicitis turns out to be suffering of a life threatening rupture of a renal artery aneurysm. We performed an emergency operation with the resection of this aneurysm. An imminent hemorrhagic shock made a targeted intensive medical therapy necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
